      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in a 2022 F-150 transmission often stem from a worn main or solenoid plunger, allowing the valve body to oscillate. You might also have low fluid level or degraded fluid causing poor lubrication and inconsistent load surfacing on the valves. It is crucial to inspect these components carefully, but given your age and high mileage, remanufacturing the transmission is likely the most cost-effective long-term solution.",
