      "content": "It is possible to be looking for a much simpler fix, as debris from clogged oil filters or degraded fluid can indeed get stuck in small solenoid orifices and cause pressure spikes. However, since you already have hydraulic pressure fluctuations running the diagnostic tool, you will need to physically clean the valve body and solenoids to check for debris and verify if they operate smoothly. Unless other major components like the clutch packs are also failing, a thorough cleaning and regeneration is likely all that is required rather than a full rebuild.",
